From 8336a876b8a142869e8a343dab0215d5b9be007c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:34:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] feat(ui): label state snapshots at capture time, and
 correct them later

Wherever the snapshot hotkey works (the environment view, recording and
inference), the page shows snapshot controls: a Defective switch, a comment
field and a Capture button, in the session side bar, and in a row above the
environment preview. Space (or its rebinding) and Capture save a snapshot with
that label, which stays for the next ones (a series of one class) and is
remembered per project in this browser (localStorage; every access may fail
without breaking anything).

- While typing in the comment field Space types; Enter or Escape leaves the
  field without reaching the page's Enter/Escape episode hotkeys.
- Within the controls Space captures also on the Defective switch and the
  buttons, instead of flipping or pressing them, so that a label never changes
  by accident; after a click there, focus goes back to the page so that Enter
  and Escape keep starting, accepting and discarding episodes.
- "Recent" lists the newest eight snapshots with their labels to correct
  (switch, comment saved on Enter or when leaving the field) and downloads the
  CSV of all snapshots.
- The toast says how the snapshot was labelled.

The capture provider now wraps the session's page (always mounted, so the page
is never mounted anew) and gives the controls the label and capture.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
